  "limitations": [
    "Subprocess transport failure is terminal and requires clean runtime/service reinitialization; normal pure computation exceptions may recover in the same child.",
    "Owner-facing sparse map reads are bounded. Dense states/probabilities/expired exports, counts and voxel_centers explicitly scan/copy the grid and can block their caller.",
    "Robot filtering assumes supported static visual meshes and static mesh-to-body placement. Detected robot model/topology/visibility changes require reinitialization; deforming models are unsupported.",
    "Supported repository GUI/native launchers use a Python interpreter. Embedded kit/kit is rejected before starting a worker; use ./run_isaac_sim.sh.",
    "Cameras must provide exposure-calibrated intrinsics/extrinsics. Native validation uses fixed world cameras; historical extrinsics for moving cameras are not reconstructed.",
    "No collision-aware controller/planner, certified collision safety, volume completion, or new perception accuracy claim follows from moving unchanged computation to subprocesses."
